WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.334 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our first guest tonight
is the co-chair

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.736 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the Bill &amp; Melinda Gate
Foundation

00:00:02.736 --> 00:00:06.272
and author of the new book "Ho
to Avoid a Climate Disaster:

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:09.642 align:start size:94% position:6%
The Solutions We Have
and the Breakthroughs We Need,

00:00:09.642 --> 00:00:10.343 size:78% position:39% line:92%
which is on sale now.

00:00:10.343 --> 00:00:12.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome to the show
Bill Gates.

00:00:12.512 --> 00:00:14.214 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How are you, Bill?

00:00:14.214 --> 00:00:15.081 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I'm great.

00:00:15.081 --> 00:00:17.183 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thanks so much
for making time for us.

00:00:17.183 --> 00:00:18.118 line:92%
I want to talk about the book.

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:21.087 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, people know you
as a philanthropist.

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:21.955 line:92%
They know you as the co-chai

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:23.590 align:start size:94% position:6%
of the Bill &amp; Melinda Gate
Foundation.

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:28.661
You also have a podcast with
my dear friend Rashida Jones

00:00:28.661 --> 00:00:30.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
Maybe not
the most obvious pairing.

00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:32.265 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How did that start?

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:36.836
-A friend from Hollywood sai
that we were complementary

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:41.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, in fact, it ended up
being a lot of fun.

00:00:41.041 --> 00:00:44.110 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, she's got
a creative background.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.545 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I do not.

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:47.147 line:92%
I'm kind of science-oriented

00:00:47.147 --> 00:00:52.419 align:start size:94% position:6%
and so we picked five topics
and went well.

00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:53.119 size:78% position:39% line:92%
-Yes, I can tell you,

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:55.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
you might not have
an entertainment background,

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:57.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
but as a friend,
she's been useless

00:00:57.991 --> 00:00:59.592 line:92%
with my computer problems,

00:00:59.592 --> 00:01:02.262 align:start size:94% position:6%
so I'm glad the two of you
found each other.

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:06.132
You know, I want to talk
a little bit about vaccine

00:01:06.132 --> 00:01:06.966 line:92%
before we move on to climate

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:09.869 size:81% position:41%
And obviously, it was
a bit of a bumpy start

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:10.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
with the rollout
here in the States.

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:13.139 size:78% position:39%
Things are obviously
looking a lot better.

00:01:13.139 --> 00:01:15.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
But you were focusing
on the importance

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:18.344 align:start size:94% position:6%
to get vaccines
into developing countries.

00:01:18.344 --> 00:01:20.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
Why do you think it's importan
for people to step back

00:01:20.447 --> 00:01:25.685
and not just look at this as a
national issue but a global one?

00:01:25.685 --> 00:01:27.087 line:92%
-Well, the first reason is

00:01:27.087 --> 00:01:29.656 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we don't want other human
to die.

00:01:29.656 --> 00:01:34.127 size:84% position:42%
And so helping them out
is morally important,

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:38.398
but also we want the world
economy to go back to normal

00:01:38.398 --> 00:01:40.333 size:78% position:39% line:92%
It creates jobs here.

00:01:40.333 --> 00:01:41.668 line:92%
And we'd also like to avoi

00:01:41.668 --> 00:01:44.804
the disease constantly returning
to our country.

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:47.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
If we can actually get it
to super-low numbers

00:01:47.440 --> 00:01:50.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
everywhere in the world
or even to zero,

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:55.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
then tourism, travel,
all these things can resume,

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:57.217 line:92%
which is very, very important.

00:01:57.217 --> 00:01:59.819 size:75% position:38%
And so we're kind of
all in it together

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:03.556 align:start size:94% position:6%
because, you know,
people travel a lot,

00:02:03.556 --> 00:02:07.861 line:92%
and we can share these vaccine

00:02:07.861 --> 00:02:11.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
not just based on
who has the most money.

00:02:11.464 --> 00:02:13.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You talk about how
we're all in this together

00:02:13.533 --> 00:02:16.636 align:start size:94% position:6%
and you're someone who,
over the course of your career

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:19.005
has tried very hard to wor
with people across the aisle

00:02:19.005 --> 00:02:20.907 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think you've looked at it as
you know,

00:02:20.907 --> 00:02:22.008 align:start size:94% position:6%
we have to put aside
our differences

00:02:22.008 --> 00:02:25.712
when we're talking about thing
that are for the greater good.

00:02:25.712 --> 00:02:29.315 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yet it also seems like science
specifically,

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
has been politicized more
maybe in this year

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:34.254 align:start size:94% position:6%
than at any point
in my lifetime.

00:02:34.254 --> 00:02:36.589 line:92%
Do you find that depressin

00:02:36.589 --> 00:02:39.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you try to move forward
with this?

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:43.062 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it's sad that
the U.S. response was so poor.

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:47.267
People had expected it to be one
of the best in the world.

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:48.635 line:92%
And in one respect it was good

00:02:48.635 --> 00:02:51.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
We funded a lot
of this vaccine work.

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:53.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
Of these first five vaccines
four of them,

00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.675 line:92%
there were big amounts of mone

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:59.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the BARDA department
of the government.

00:02:59.579 --> 00:03:03.683 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that's now showing us
that this will come to an end.

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:05.518 line:92%
These vaccines are miracles.

00:03:05.518 --> 00:03:10.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank God that the private
sector, with government money,

00:03:10.657 --> 00:03:12.192 line:92%
has pulled these together.

00:03:12.192 --> 00:03:16.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
But in other respects the last
year has been frustrating

00:03:16.696 --> 00:03:21.134 align:start size:94% position:6%
because the willingness
to push guidelines

00:03:21.134 --> 00:03:22.535 line:92%
and admit that things are tough,

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:26.639 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, the ability
to show leadership on masks,

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:32.045 align:start size:94% position:6%
and now encouraging
vaccine uptake.

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:35.848
You know, I think the U.S.
has a lot to look back on

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:41.354 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, you know, figure out
that when this comes next time

00:03:41.354 --> 00:03:42.922 size:78% position:39% line:92%
we have to do better.

00:03:42.922 --> 00:03:46.593
-You know, obviously in the last
week we've seen states --

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:49.295 align:start size:94% position:6%
Texas, Mississippi
as a couple of examples --

00:03:49.295 --> 00:03:52.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
they are now, you know,
from the governor's office dow

00:03:52.232 --> 00:03:54.834 align:start size:94% position:6%
rescinding the statewide
masks orders.

00:03:54.834 --> 00:03:56.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that something
that you find distressing,

00:03:56.135 --> 00:04:00.173
especially after everything yo
would have hoped we've learned

00:04:00.173 --> 00:04:01.474 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
in the last year?

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:03.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, I just don't think
wearing a mask

00:04:03.843 --> 00:04:05.378 line:92%
is such a deep inconvenience

00:04:05.378 --> 00:04:08.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, we ask people
to wear pants.

00:04:08.548 --> 00:04:12.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, why was this
politicized?

00:04:12.919 --> 00:04:14.454 size:78% position:39% line:92%
The mask helps a lot.

00:04:14.454 --> 00:04:18.825
And although we're near the end,
every death is tragic.

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:21.194 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Now I feel terrible
about the fact that I --

00:04:21.194 --> 00:04:23.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
I should admit
I'm not wearing pants now.

00:04:23.863 --> 00:04:24.864 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:29.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, don't go outside.
You might infect somebody.

00:04:29.135 --> 00:04:31.337 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-[ Laughs ]

